OBJECTIVES:

1. To develop a menu-driven Water Depot Network System for finding the
shortest route to repair locations efficiently.
2. To store location details such as location name, location type (water
depot, road junction or repair location) and connected roads in a graph
using an adjacency list.
3. To perform essential operations such as adding new locations, adding
roads between locations, searching for locations and displaying the
network.
4. To apply Dijkstra's algorithm to find the least-cost route from the
water depot to a selected repair location and display the route and total
distance.
5. To use a min-priority queue for always selecting the nearest unvisited
location and helping reduce unnecessary calculations.
6. To use a parent array to trace the route from the repair location back
to the source and display the location sequence.
7. To apply non-negative distances (in km) as edge weights so that
Dijkstra's algorithm gives correct shortest paths.
8. To select a different source vertex and recalculate the shortest
distances to all locations (Modification A).
9. To improve accuracy, accessibility, and organization of repair route
planning while reducing manual route-finding effort.
